'\"macro stdmacro
.TH PMDADB2LOCAL 1 "PCP" "Performance Co-Pilot"
.SH NAME
\f3pmdadb2local\f1 \- local IBM Db2 command-line PMDA
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmdadb2local collects local IBM Db2 state with \fBdb2level\fP,
\fBdb2pd\fP and \fBdb2diag\fP.  It does not open network connections, use SQL,
require database credentials, or use the \fBibm_db\fP Python module.
.PP
The focused metric set includes \fBdb2local.instance\fP identity, member state
and uptime, \fBdb2local.agent\fP counts, database-scoped buffer pool sizing and
tablespace capacity, and cached \fBdb2local.diag\fP counts.  Diagnostic
counts use \fBdb2diag -gi level=severe|error -H 15m -c\fP and are cached for ten
minutes, retried at most once per ten minutes, and withheld once the last
successful count is twenty minutes old; log them at a 10 to 15 minute interval.
.PP
The metrics are chosen for what the local tools add over \fBpmdadb2\fP:
instance state and agent counts without a database connection, static
buffer pool and tablespace capacity that SQL monitoring views do not expose,
and diagnostic-log counts that remain available when the database engine is
unresponsive.  Buffer pool I/O counters and tablespace I/O aggregates are
already provided by \fBpmdadb2\fP and are not duplicated here.
.PP
This first release deliberately limits live collection to the following metric
groups: \fBinstance\fP, \fBagent\fP, \fBbufferpool\fP, \fBtablespace\fP,
and \fBdiag\fP. Buffer pool and tablespace instance names are
\fIdatabase::object\fP and provide corresponding PCP labels.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The mandatory INI file is \fI$PCP_SYSCONF_DIR/db2local/db2local.conf\fP.
The \fB[db2]\fP section accepts \fBbin_dir\fP (default
\fI/opt/ibm/db2/V11.5/bin\fP), \fBuser\fP (\fIdb2inst1\fP), and \fBprofile\fP
(\fI~/sqllib/db2profile\fP). Paths must resolve to absolute paths. Only a
leading \fB~/\fP is accepted in either path and is expanded using the configured
Db2 user's home directory.
.PP
Database aliases and their catalog database names are rediscovered when
database-scoped buffer pool or tablespace metrics are refreshed.  Instance
names use the alias, while \fBdb2pd -db\fP is given the database name, which
may differ.  Rediscovery is briefly cached to avoid duplicating local CLP
calls in a single fetch.
.PP
The agent is started through the normal privileged \fBpmdaroot\fP path,
initializes the configured account groups and permanently changes to that
user.  The profile is sourced on first use, after the agent has connected to
\fBpmcd\fP, and only validated programs below \fBbin_dir\fP or the
instance-home \fBsqllib/adm\fP directory (where \fBdb2pd\fP is installed) are
executed.  If it cannot make this transition it fails without running Db2
commands.  Db2 must be installed on the PMDA host.
.SH INSTALLATION
\fBpmdaroot\fP must be installed and active so this transition can occur.
As root, run \fB$PCP_PMDAS_DIR/db2local/Install\fP. Remove it with
\fB$PCP_PMDAS_DIR/db2local/Remove\fP.
.SH LIMITATIONS
This is not metric-compatible with \fBpmdadb2\fP. SQL-only database-wide
transaction, row, CPU and wait counters, complete connection activity, latch
wait totals, tablespace I/O aggregates, transaction-log I/O totals, and package
cache statement CPU, execution, row and sort statistics are deliberately absent.
.PP
The command-line groups \fBapplication\fP, \fBedu\fP, \fBlock\fP,
\fBlatch\fP, \fBlog\fP, \fBmemory\fP, \fBpackage_cache\fP,
\fBworkload\fP, \fBserviceclass\fP, \fButility\fP, \fBrecovery\fP,
\fBhadr\fP, \fBreorg\fP, and \fBstorage\fP are deferred. Additional
buffer-pool I/O fields and tablespace high-water-mark, state, and auto-resize
fields are also deferred. In particular, no one-second EDU sampling is performed.
.PP
On a multi-member instance \fBdb2pd\fP reports one member per command. This
release reports the local member only and does not aggregate values across
members; run one PMDA per member host if member-wide views are required.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $PCP_SYSCONF_DIR/db2local/db2local.conf
Db2 instance-user and local command configuration.
.TP
.I $PCP_PMDAS_DIR/db2local
PMDA program and installation scripts.
.TP
.I $PCP_SYSCONF_DIR/pmlogconf/db2local
pmlogconf group templates.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pmcd (1),
.BR pmdadb2 (1)
